      "id": "OC-1",
      "severity": "closed-was-architecture-blocking-for-macOS-credentials",
      "statement": "The macOS packet-tunnel system extension runs as root in a non-user context. The Data Protection Keychain is available only to code running in a user context, and keychain access groups share items between programs running as the SAME user. The .spec/security-privacy.md design — private keys and passphrases in the Data Protection Keychain shared through one access group with the packet tunnel extension — therefore CANNOT work between the macOS host and the macOS provider. It works unchanged on iOS.",
      "corroboration": "Observed 2026-07-28 on this Mac. (a) Two shipping Developer ID packet-tunnel system extensions ship com.apple.security.temporary-exception.files.absolute-path.read-write entries for /private/var/root/Library/Group Containers/ (Tailscale, Surfshark) — direct evidence that a root provider's group container is not the user's. (b) Surfshark's provider carries a temporary-exception path for /Library/Keychains/, i.e. the FILE-BASED System keychain, not the Data Protection Keychain. (c) PureVPN's providers carry keychain-access-groups outright. Together these indicate the real-world macOS pattern is a file-based/System keychain or an IPC seed, not a shared Data Protection Keychain access group.",
      "affects": [
        "TASK-260715-1o9wjz",
        "TASK-260715-379cpk",
